|> Exercise
    work=ing
    handle=_how_many_bumps_

    If the graph below has three “bumps” (two up,
    one down), then how many “bumps” does its derivative
    have?

    |> Image
        src=images/how_many_bumps_statement.svg
        style=padding-bottom:1rem

    |> Solution

        The derivative has a “bump” wherever the slope
        has a local maximum or local minimum, which happens
        at four places:

        |> Image
            src=images/how_many_bumps_statement_with_highlights.svg

        !! |> Image
        !!     src=images/how_many_bumps_statement_with_derivative.svg